docs {
  ## Get Application Details
  
  This endpoint retrieves a list of applications associated with the player app.
  
  ### Request
  
  - **Method**: GET
      
  - **URL**: `{{baseUrl}}/api/playerapp/getapp`
      
  
  ### Response
  
  - **Status Code**: 200 OK
      
  - **Content-Type**: application/json
      
  
  #### Response Body
  
  The response will return an array of application objects, each containing the following fields:
  
  - `appId`: (string) The unique identifier for the application.
      
  - `appName`: (string) The name of the application.
      
  - `appDescription`: (string) A brief description of the application.
      
  - `githubUrl`: (string) The URL to the application's GitHub repository.
      
  - `currentVersion`: (string) The current version of the application.
      
  - `dateCreated`: (string) The date when the application was created.
      
  - `dateUpdated`: (string|null) The date when the application was last updated. This field may be null if the application has not been updated.
      
  
  ### Notes
  
  - Ensure that the request is made to the correct base URL.
      
  - The response will be an array, even if there is only one application.
      
  - Handle cases where fields may be empty or null in your application logic.
}
